{"decision": "MUST_FIX", "summary": "Reviewed requested source at 3a1a589; the six primary files are unchanged at workspace HEAD 86a334c. Verified actual snapshot 0add4b0 against its receipt: source hashes and tracked diff match, no writable entries or symlinks, and no untracked files reported. Initial source-config and snapshot test failures are fixture issues, not implementation defects. Found source-binding, replay, and dispatcher recovery defects below. No files changed or write-producing tests run; counterexamples used in-memory substitutes only. This review grants no compatibility, live, capacity, or scientific approval.", "evidence_pins": [{"path": "training_workloads/unified_h1/config.py", "sha256": "6fa2d2fd8d3e11af3bdd1fda2c9816680d6b155d78ea7654ac7f294147386086"}, {"path": "training_workloads/unified_h1/authorization.py", "sha256": "efa536c680db19d9cc3697f4c629183759fae51af17f9e16bc66c0456e71e02b"}, {"path": "tools/prepare_r6_snapshot.py", "sha256": "dbe09c02f631e61e5b2d05915f3a5a349f9928658417460cd3d420875a0dd3f8"}, {"path": "training_workloads/unified_h1/local_dispatch.py", "sha256": "5b24935d192a8e1e6e607f09543b7dd494ff5fb227625f34d2f8d9e9f664792e"}, {"path": "tools/rlflow/rlflow/experiments.py", "sha256": "dd85dee9971a93137348320364c82a95f377d4e963e649262df5bfd3157a937d"}, {"path": "tools/rlflow/rlflow/h1.py", "sha256": "f8cfc2a16c01c7003dd8914755ddec922c7b2865801ac68f8689f29e24aea238"}, {"path": "docs/experiments/r6-robustness-auto/batch/snapshots/dac0f3d535ca1c68d0764a7bbc34b3bb2921590c46e1f86747785ca3a978395e/receipt.json", "sha256": "3ae074fed7e56feaf684bdd467149adc1fad96b1d4dd70d6c4b6a83168dbf5a0"}, {"path": "docs/experiments/r6-robustness-auto/CPU_R6_SOURCE_CONFIG_TESTS.json", "sha256": "99395e4c0530e9af2ebdb77772523c7b0f2a769606d7d1833a30828bf761ed90"}, {"path": "docs/experiments/r6-robustness-auto/CPU_R6_SNAPSHOT_VERIFICATION.json", "sha256": "3dd9551c760957463a720b9d6345112aae3aea054c6a15e23ac9d7a6ca737b76"}, {"path": "docs/experiments/r6-robustness-auto/CPU_R6_NATIVE_OUTPUT_TESTS.json", "sha256": "626a382bfc038c438e718d1a891562db2c06952ab09936aec5ec585d36e38c19"}], "changed_files": [], "next_plan": "Repair these defects and add focused CPU regression evidence before independent re-review. Preserve snapshot 0add4b0 and its receipt; later changes require a new exact snapshot and control release. Independent compatibility approval, complete filesystem/native/cache/crash capacity bounds, protocol freeze, Store issuance, full controller integration, and scientific validation remain pending. Full capacity remains false. Parent records actual session receipt usage.", "remaining_budget": {"automatic_sessions_remaining": 26}, "must_fix": ["SOURCE CLOSURE — training_workloads/unified_h1/config.py: R6_PRODUCT_SOURCES/R6_WORKLOAD_SOURCES omit executable local dependencies. For example, robustness_audit.write_block_metadata imports training_workloads/scale_003/config.py, also imported by the pinned persistence.py; scale_003/__init__.py imports schedule.py. Product observations/__init__.py imports observations/audit.py. These files are absent from the manifests. Substituting their bytes leaves HEAD/tree and every checked source hash unchanged; _validate_repository does not reject other working-tree changes, and validate_loaded_module_origins does not hash these dependencies. Minimal remedy: add the executable dependency closure to the R6-only manifests and exercise individual substitutions, preserving historical schema sets.", "SNAPSHOT REPLAY — tools/prepare_r6_snapshot.py:verify_frozen, lines 58–71, checks tracked git diff and selected hashes but never checks the complete checkout inventory. An added read-only untracked sitecustomize.py passes these checks and can execute on the configured Python startup through PYTHONPATH; ignored bytecode is another unverified input. An in-memory overlay adding a read-only untracked entry was accepted by the actual verify_frozen function. Symlinks are also skipped by its permission check. Minimal remedy: record and verify the complete execution-tree inventory, including unexpected/ignored files and file types; reject unapproved additions and symlinks. The actual inspected snapshot was clean; this is a replay-validation defect.", "FAILURE EVIDENCE LOSS — training_workloads/unified_h1/local_dispatch.py:dispatch_held/_reclaim, lines 141–142 and 175–194. Handshake and cleanup waitpid calls discard observed exit status. An in-memory counterexample with cap=4, output='12345', and cleanup waitpid returning exit 7 produced native_exit_code=null despite observing exit 7. STOP/timeout cleanup also closes the output reader without draining bytes queued during termination, losing diagnostic output below the cap. Minimal remedy: retain every observed wait status, boundedly drain the remaining permitted prefix during cleanup, and preserve native exit separately from transport failure. Keep outer lifeguard responsible for descendant cleanup.", "UNRELATED PROCESS SIGNALING — training_workloads/unified_h1/local_dispatch.py:dispatch_held handshake and _reclaim. When the handshake waitpid reaps the child, native_exit remains None and the exception path still calls _reclaim. If that PID is reused by an unrelated process-group leader, getpgid(pid)==pid passes and killpg sends SIGTERM to the unrelated group. The in-memory syscall substitute demonstrated this signaling path. Minimal remedy: track reaped ownership explicitly, never reclaim a reaped PID, and preserve its exit status; do not infer ownership merely from numerical PID/PGID equality.", "SETUP RESOURCE LEAK — training_workloads/unified_h1/local_dispatch.py:dispatch_held, lines 98–121. Native log/pipe creation, identity/release pipes, fork, and selector registration occur before the cleanup try/finally. A fork EAGAIN leaks pipe descriptors and leaves an exclusive native-output.log without a failure receipt; selector setup failure after fork can leave the child held with the release writer still open. Minimal remedy: establish cleanup protection before acquiring resources, track each descriptor and successful fork, close all acquired endpoints on setup failure, and preserve a failure receipt when possible without automatic retry."]}
